  #sol-item(1, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.82pt)[
    B — a collective noun acting as one body takes a singular verb, so has. Have and are would treat the committee as separate members, and were is past tense, which the sentence does not allow.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.82pt)[
    C — a fraction takes its number from the noun after of, and land is uncountable and singular, so is. Are, were and have been all need a plural noun such as plots or acres.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "A", dense: true, pad: 15.82pt)[
    D — the head of the subject is list, singular, and every of-phrase after it is a passenger, so was. Were and are would agree with names or candidates rather than with the head.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.82pt)[
    B — neither is singular however many candidates follow it, so meets. Meet and are meeting would need a plural subject such as both candidates.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "B", dense: true, pad: 15.82pt)[
    B — a number of means several and takes a plural verb: were. Was, is and has been would all make a number a single count, which is the meaning of the number of.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "B", dense: true, pad: 15.82pt)[
    C — the number of means the count itself, which is singular, so is. Are, were and have been agree with students rather than with number.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "D", dense: true, pad: 15.82pt)[
    D — each is singular, so the verb is was. Were, have been and are would all need a plural subject.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 15.82pt)[
    B — every one is singular, so the verb is was. The phrase of the girls does not change the number of the head.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 15.82pt)[
